# The runtime exclude list — what the release tarball carries and what stays out.
#
# pack-app.sh (the org's shared app-release workflow, instalador #31) reads this file
# with rsync rules anchored at the app root, and it REPLACES the packer's defaults, so
# it must list every development path itself; '!' re-include lines are refused. The
# tarball carries appinfo/, js/ (built by the release), lib/, templates/, img/, seeds/
# (the Metas Sanitarias the migrations load at enable — runtime data, not repo
# material), vendor/aps/common/src, LICENSE and README.md — an install needs no build
# step and no development tree.
#
# src/ needs no re-include for src/aps: the vendored aps-common code is build input,
# bundled into js/ by the release build, and nothing at runtime reads it.
# vendor/ needs no rule: the release packs a fresh checkout, which holds only what git
# tracks under it (aps/common/src — .gitignore keeps composer's installed extras out),
# and nothing in the release runs composer.
# /.* covers every dotfile and dot directory at the root, this file included:
# .github, .githooks, .gitignore, .graphifyignore, .htaccess (a guard for a dev
# checkout's repo material; the tarball ships none of what it denies).
- /.*
- /src
- /tests
- /docs
- /scripts
- /tools
- /CHANGELOG.md
- /openapi.json
- /AGENTS.md
- /CONTEXT.md
- /Makefile
- /package.json
- /package-lock.json
- /composer.json
- /composer.lock
- /phpunit.xml
- /phpunit.integration.xml
- /eslint.config.mjs
- /vitest.config.ts
- /webpack.config.js
- /Dockerfile.test
- /compose.dev.yaml
# Sourcemaps stay out of the tarball (.gitignore's rule for the repo, this one for
# the release): they name every source path of the build machine.
- /js/*.map
